1
00:00:02,509 --> 00:00:03,760
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04,886 --> 00:00:06,137
Earth...

3
00:00:06,846 --> 00:00:08,139
Fire...

4
00:00:08,848 --> 00:00:10,183
Air.

5
00:00:11,017 --> 00:00:14,229
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,146 --> 00:00:19,067
Then everything changed
when the fire nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:23,613
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

8
00:00:23,696 --> 00:00:25,448
But when the world
needed him most

9
00:00:25,532 --> 00:00:27,408
he vanished.

10
00:00:27,492 --> 00:00:31,079
100 years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

11
00:00:31,162 --> 00:00:32,789
an Airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:32,872 --> 00:00:35,208
And although his airbending
skills are great

13
00:00:35,291 --> 00:00:37,669
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,752 --> 00:00:38,753
AANG: Oof.

15
00:00:38,878 --> 00:00:42,882
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

16
00:00:42,966 --> 00:00:46,469
[ ♪... ]

17
00:00:48,054 --> 00:00:50,515
( MAN READING )

18
00:00:50,598 --> 00:00:54,435
You're looking at the only Waterbender
in the whole south pole.

19
00:00:55,228 --> 00:00:58,523
This ship has haunted my tribe
since gran-gran was a little girl.

20
00:00:58,606 --> 00:01:01,985
It was part of
the Fire Nation's first attack.

21
00:01:02,068 --> 00:01:05,280
WOMAN: The legends say the moon
was the first Waterbender.

22
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:07,615
Our ancestors saw how it
pushed and pulled the tides

23
00:01:07,699 --> 00:01:09,867
and learned how to
do it themselves.

24
00:01:09,951 --> 00:01:13,037
KATARA: I've always noticed
my waterbending is stronger at night.

25
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:17,041
TOPH: What are you doing?

26
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:19,252
KATARA: I'm making my own water.

27
00:01:22,005 --> 00:01:24,424
[ ♪... ]

28
00:01:27,302 --> 00:01:29,220
[ Crickets Chirping... ]

29
00:01:38,771 --> 00:01:41,608
Suddenly, they heard something
down the hall, in the dark.

30
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,570
♪Ooh... ♪

31
00:01:46,154 --> 00:01:48,698
It came into the torchlight.

32
00:01:49,365 --> 00:01:53,119
And they knew the blade
of Wing-fun was haunted!

33
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:57,957
♪Ah-ah... ♪

34
00:01:59,083 --> 00:02:02,462
I think I liked "The Man
With a Sword for a Hand" better.

35
00:02:02,545 --> 00:02:05,298
Water tribe slumber parties
must stink.

36
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,383
No, wait, I've got one.

37
00:02:07,467 --> 00:02:09,844
And this is a true southern
Water tribe story.

38
00:02:10,136 --> 00:02:11,888
Is this one of those
"a friend of my cousin

39
00:02:11,971 --> 00:02:14,557
knew some guy that
this happened to" story?

40
00:02:14,849 --> 00:02:17,268
No, it happened to Mom.

41
00:02:20,146 --> 00:02:22,315
One winter, when Mom was a girl

42
00:02:22,398 --> 00:02:25,234
a snowstorm buried
the whole village for weeks.

43
00:02:25,318 --> 00:02:29,572
A month later, mom realized she hadn't
seen her friend Nini since the storm.

44
00:02:29,656 --> 00:02:32,784
So Mom and some others
went to check on Nini's family.

45
00:02:32,867 --> 00:02:34,911
When they got there,
no one was home.

46
00:02:34,994 --> 00:02:37,580
Just a fire
flickering in the fireplace.

47
00:02:37,664 --> 00:02:39,624
While the men
went out to search

48
00:02:39,707 --> 00:02:41,167
Mom stayed in the house.

49
00:02:41,250 --> 00:02:44,253
When she was alone,
she heard a voice.

50
00:02:44,337 --> 00:02:48,925
"It's so cold,
and I can't get warm."

51
00:02:49,008 --> 00:02:52,178
Mom turned and saw
Nini standing by the fire.

52
00:02:52,261 --> 00:02:54,681
She was blue,
like she was frozen.

53
00:02:54,764 --> 00:02:58,643
Mom ran outside for help,
but when every one came back

54
00:02:58,726 --> 00:03:00,561
Nini was gone.

55
00:03:00,853 --> 00:03:02,355
SOKKA: Where'd she go?

56
00:03:02,772 --> 00:03:04,148
No one knows.

57
00:03:04,232 --> 00:03:06,901
Nini's house stands empty
to this day.

58
00:03:06,984 --> 00:03:09,904
But sometimes, people see smoke
coming up from the chimney

59
00:03:09,987 --> 00:03:13,491
like little Nini is still
trying to get warm.

60
00:03:16,911 --> 00:03:18,538
[ Gasps ]
Wait.

61
00:03:18,621 --> 00:03:20,707
Guys, did you hear that?

62
00:03:20,998 --> 00:03:24,377
I hear people under the mountain,
and they're screaming.

63
00:03:25,670 --> 00:03:27,463
Pft, nice try.

64
00:03:27,839 --> 00:03:30,675
TOPH: No, I'm serious,
I hear something.

65
00:03:30,758 --> 00:03:33,886
KATARA: You're probably just
jumpy from the ghost stories.

66
00:03:34,554 --> 00:03:36,305
TOPH: It just stopped.

67
00:03:36,389 --> 00:03:38,516
All right, now
I'm getting scared.

68
00:03:38,933 --> 00:03:40,351
WOMAN: Hello, children.

69
00:03:40,435 --> 00:03:42,145
[ Screaming ]

70
00:03:44,939 --> 00:03:48,151
Sorry to frighten you,
my name is Hama.

71
00:03:48,234 --> 00:03:52,238
You children shouldn't be out in
the forest by yourselves at night.

72
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:56,117
I have an inn nearby,
why don't you come back there

73
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,327
for some spiced tea and warm beds?

74
00:03:59,162 --> 00:04:00,997
Yes, please.

75
00:04:08,296 --> 00:04:11,215
Thanks for letting us stay here tonight,
you have a lovely inn.

76
00:04:11,299 --> 00:04:13,176
Aren't you sweet?

77
00:04:13,259 --> 00:04:14,886
You know, you should be careful.

78
00:04:14,969 --> 00:04:18,473
People have been disappearing in
those woods you were camping in.

79
00:04:18,806 --> 00:04:20,475
What do you mean, disappearing?

80
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:25,146
When the moon turns full,
people walk in

81
00:04:25,229 --> 00:04:28,399
and they don't come out.

82
00:04:28,483 --> 00:04:30,860
Who wants more tea?

83
00:04:34,822 --> 00:04:38,201
Don't worry, you'll all be
completely safe here.

84
00:04:38,284 --> 00:04:43,039
Why don't I show you to your rooms,
and you can get a good night's rest?

85
00:04:45,291 --> 00:04:47,084
[ Wood Creaks ]

86
00:04:47,168 --> 00:04:48,669
[ Grunts ]

87
00:04:48,878 --> 00:04:50,546
[ Wood Creaks ]

88
00:04:51,172 --> 00:04:52,673
[ Gasps ]

89
00:04:53,591 --> 00:04:55,927
I know, Momo,
this place is creepy.

90
00:04:56,135 --> 00:04:58,471
I don't know if I'm
gonna be able to fall asleep.

91
00:04:59,055 --> 00:05:02,058
[ Snoring... ]

92
00:05:04,852 --> 00:05:07,063
[ Birds Chirping ]

93
00:05:08,564 --> 00:05:10,566
HAMA: Wakey-wakey.

94
00:05:11,108 --> 00:05:13,402
Time to go shopping.

95
00:05:23,663 --> 00:05:25,957
That Mr. Yao seems to
have a thing for you.

96
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:29,293
Maybe we should go back and see if he'll
give us some free komodo sausages.

97
00:05:29,877 --> 00:05:33,256
You would have me use
my feminine charms

98
00:05:33,339 --> 00:05:35,591
to take advantage
of that poor man?

99
00:05:35,675 --> 00:05:39,428
I think you and I are
going to get along swimmingly.

100
00:05:39,512 --> 00:05:42,557
You won't have any
ash bananas till next week?

101
00:05:43,349 --> 00:05:46,561
Well, I have to send the boy
to Hing-wa Island to get them,

102
00:05:46,644 --> 00:05:47,687
and it's a two-day trip.

103
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:51,148
Oh, right, tomorrow's
the full moon.

104
00:05:51,232 --> 00:05:54,485
Exactly, I can't lose another
delivery boy in the woods.

105
00:05:55,236 --> 00:05:57,154
People disappearing
in the woods,

106
00:05:57,238 --> 00:05:59,031
weird stuff during full moons,

107
00:05:59,115 --> 00:06:01,826
this just reeks of
spirit world shenanigans.

108
00:06:01,909 --> 00:06:04,245
I bet if we take
a little walk around town

109
00:06:04,328 --> 00:06:07,498
we'll find out what these people did to
the environment to make the spirits mad.

110
00:06:07,582 --> 00:06:11,669
And then you can sew up this little
mystery, lickety-split, Avatar-style.

111
00:06:11,752 --> 00:06:14,213
Helping people,
that's what I do.

112
00:06:15,089 --> 00:06:18,384
HAMA: Why don't you all take
those things back to the inn?

113
00:06:18,551 --> 00:06:20,761
I just have to run
a couple more errands.

114
00:06:20,845 --> 00:06:22,930
I'll be back in a little while.

115
00:06:23,389 --> 00:06:25,391
This is a mysterious,
little town you have here.

116
00:06:26,517 --> 00:06:29,770
Mysterious town
for mysterious children.

117
00:06:36,986 --> 00:06:38,946
That Hama seems a little strange.

118
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:41,574
Like she knows something,
or she's hiding something.

119
00:06:41,657 --> 00:06:43,284
That's ridiculous.

120
00:06:43,367 --> 00:06:46,412
She's a nice woman who took us
in and gave us a place to stay.

121
00:06:46,495 --> 00:06:48,122
She kind of reminds me
of gran-gran.

122
00:06:48,497 --> 00:06:51,584
But what did she mean by that comment
"mysterious children"?

123
00:06:51,876 --> 00:06:53,294
Gee, I don't know.

124
00:06:53,377 --> 00:06:57,340
Maybe because she found four strange kids
camping in the woods at night?

125
00:06:57,673 --> 00:07:00,217
Isn't that a little mysterious?

126
00:07:00,551 --> 00:07:02,887
I'm gonna take a look around.

127
00:07:05,556 --> 00:07:07,850
Sokka, Sokka,
what are you doing?

128
00:07:07,934 --> 00:07:10,311
You can't just snoop around
someone's house.

129
00:07:10,394 --> 00:07:11,395
SOKKA: It'll be fine.

130
00:07:11,479 --> 00:07:14,023
AANG: She could be home
any minute.

131
00:07:14,982 --> 00:07:17,526
Sokka, you're gonna get us
all in trouble.

132
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:19,320
And this is just plain rude.

133
00:07:19,403 --> 00:07:20,863
I'm not finished yet.

134
00:07:20,988 --> 00:07:23,491
[ Grunts ]
Come on...

135
00:07:24,867 --> 00:07:27,036
[ Screams ]

136
00:07:27,119 --> 00:07:29,288
AANG: Ok, that's pretty creepy.

137
00:07:29,538 --> 00:07:31,374
So she's got a hobby.

138
00:07:31,457 --> 00:07:32,917
There's nothing
weird about that.

139
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,794
Sokka, you've looked enough.

140
00:07:34,877 --> 00:07:36,587
Hama will be back soon.

141
00:07:36,671 --> 00:07:38,089
[ Sokka Grunts ]

142
00:07:38,172 --> 00:07:40,257
Just an ordinary, puppet-loving
innkeeper, huh?

143
00:07:40,341 --> 00:07:42,218
Then why does she have
a locked door up here?

144
00:07:42,301 --> 00:07:45,763
Probably to keep people like you
from snooping through her stuff.

145
00:07:45,846 --> 00:07:47,974
SOKKA: We'll see.

146
00:07:48,057 --> 00:07:49,809
It's empty except for
a little chest.

147
00:07:49,892 --> 00:07:53,396
[ Gasps ]
Maybe it's treasure.

148
00:07:53,479 --> 00:07:55,439
Sokka, what are you doing?

149
00:07:55,523 --> 00:07:57,400
You're breaking into
a private room.

150
00:07:57,483 --> 00:07:59,735
I have to see what's in there.

151
00:08:02,905 --> 00:08:05,408
We shouldn't be doing this.

152
00:08:05,908 --> 00:08:08,160
Maybe there's a key
here somewhere.

153
00:08:08,244 --> 00:08:09,996
Oh, hand it over.

154
00:08:14,709 --> 00:08:16,335
Come on, come on.

155
00:08:16,419 --> 00:08:18,546
This isn't as easy it looks.

156
00:08:18,879 --> 00:08:20,631
AANG: Guys, I don't know
about this.

157
00:08:20,715 --> 00:08:22,800
This is crazy, I'm leaving.

158
00:08:22,883 --> 00:08:24,677
Suit yourself, do it, Toph.

159
00:08:28,305 --> 00:08:30,599
HAMA: I'll tell you
what's in the box.

160
00:08:45,781 --> 00:08:47,450
An old comb?

161
00:08:47,533 --> 00:08:50,453
It's my greatest treasure.

162
00:08:50,536 --> 00:08:55,041
It's the last thing I owned from
growing up in the southern Water tribe.

163
00:08:59,712 --> 00:09:01,714
You're from the southern
Water tribe?

164
00:09:02,548 --> 00:09:03,883
Just like you.

165
00:09:03,966 --> 00:09:05,301
How did you know?

166
00:09:05,384 --> 00:09:07,678
I heard you talking
around your campfire.

167
00:09:07,762 --> 00:09:09,597
But why didn't you tell us?

168
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:11,766
I wanted to surprise you.

169
00:09:11,849 --> 00:09:16,479
I bought all this food today so I could
fix you a big, Water Tribe dinner.

170
00:09:16,729 --> 00:09:19,899
Of course, I can't get all
the ingredients I need here, but

171
00:09:20,066 --> 00:09:24,195
ocean kumquats are a lot like sea prunes,
if you stew them long enough.

172
00:09:24,278 --> 00:09:25,404
[ Gags ]

173
00:09:25,488 --> 00:09:26,530
Great.

174
00:09:26,655 --> 00:09:28,824
I knew I felt a bond
with you right away.

175
00:09:29,241 --> 00:09:30,910
And I knew you were
keeping a secret

176
00:09:30,993 --> 00:09:32,828
so I guess we're both right.

177
00:09:32,912 --> 00:09:35,748
[ Grunts ] But I'm sorry we were
sneaking around.

178
00:09:35,915 --> 00:09:37,625
Apology accepted.

179
00:09:38,501 --> 00:09:40,127
Now let's get cooking.

180
00:09:49,970 --> 00:09:52,556
[ Momo Chirps ]

181
00:09:59,563 --> 00:10:01,941
I'd steer clear
of the sea prunes.

182
00:10:02,066 --> 00:10:04,360
I thought they were
ocean kumquats.

183
00:10:04,443 --> 00:10:05,528
Close enough.

184
00:10:05,653 --> 00:10:08,447
Who wants five-flavor soup?

185
00:10:13,452 --> 00:10:14,578
You're a Waterbender.

186
00:10:14,662 --> 00:10:17,373
I've never met another
Waterbender from our tribe.

187
00:10:17,456 --> 00:10:21,043
That's because the Fire Nation
wiped them all out.

188
00:10:21,502 --> 00:10:23,087
I was the last one.

189
00:10:23,337 --> 00:10:25,089
So how did you end up out here?

190
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:28,592
I was stolen from my home.

191
00:10:30,052 --> 00:10:33,639
It was over 60 years ago
when the raids started.

192
00:10:34,473 --> 00:10:36,058
[ Laughing ]

193
00:10:56,203 --> 00:10:57,621
[ Man Screams ]

194
00:11:00,666 --> 00:11:02,418
HAMA: They came again and again.

195
00:11:02,793 --> 00:11:07,381
Each time, rounding up more of our
Waterbenders and taking them captive.

196
00:11:07,882 --> 00:11:10,134
[ Breathing Heavily ]

197
00:11:11,677 --> 00:11:13,470
We did our best to hold them off

198
00:11:13,554 --> 00:11:17,558
but our numbers dwindled
as the raids continued.

199
00:11:25,649 --> 00:11:29,236
Finally, I, too, was captured.

200
00:11:30,821 --> 00:11:33,032
I was led away in chains.

201
00:11:34,450 --> 00:11:38,454
The last Waterbender of
the southern Water Tribe.

202
00:11:45,461 --> 00:11:49,256
They put us in terrible prisons
here in the Fire Nation.

203
00:11:49,590 --> 00:11:52,968
I was the only one
who managed to escape.

204
00:11:53,052 --> 00:11:54,595
How did you get away?

205
00:11:54,678 --> 00:11:56,472
And why did you stay
in the Fire Nation?

206
00:11:57,097 --> 00:11:58,557
I'm sorry.

207
00:11:58,641 --> 00:12:01,727
It's too painful to
talk about anymore.

208
00:12:01,810 --> 00:12:03,687
We completely understand.

209
00:12:03,771 --> 00:12:05,898
We lost our mother in a raid.

210
00:12:06,232 --> 00:12:08,525
Oh, you poor things.

211
00:12:10,945 --> 00:12:13,447
I can't tell you
what it means to meet you.

212
00:12:13,530 --> 00:12:15,950
It's an honor, you're a hero.

213
00:12:16,325 --> 00:12:19,536
I never thought I'd meet
another southern Waterbender.

214
00:12:19,787 --> 00:12:21,830
I'd like to teach you
what I know

215
00:12:21,914 --> 00:12:25,167
so you can carry on the southern tradition
when I'm gone.

216
00:12:25,584 --> 00:12:28,379
Yes, yes, of course.

217
00:12:28,837 --> 00:12:32,258
To learn about my heritage,
it would mean everything to me.

218
00:12:36,845 --> 00:12:38,889
HAMA: Growing up
at the south pole

219
00:12:38,973 --> 00:12:43,852
Waterbenders are totally at home
surrounded by snow and ice and seas.

220
00:12:44,395 --> 00:12:46,897
But as you probably
noticed on your travels,

221
00:12:46,981 --> 00:12:49,233
that isn't the case
wherever you go.

222
00:12:49,483 --> 00:12:51,819
I know, when we were
stranded in the desert

223
00:12:51,902 --> 00:12:54,571
I felt like there was
almost nothing I could do.

224
00:12:54,655 --> 00:12:58,659
That's why you have to learn to
control water wherever it exists.

225
00:12:58,951 --> 00:13:01,537
I've even used my own
sweat for waterbending.

226
00:13:01,704 --> 00:13:04,081
That's very resourceful, Katara.

227
00:13:04,206 --> 00:13:06,583
You're thinking like
a true master.

228
00:13:06,667 --> 00:13:10,045
But did you know you can even
pull water out of thin air?

229
00:13:14,258 --> 00:13:17,303
You've got to
keep an open mind, Katara.

230
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:21,056
There's water in places
you never think about.

231
00:13:25,644 --> 00:13:28,689
AANG: This has gotta be the nicest,
natural setting in the Fire Nation.

232
00:13:29,023 --> 00:13:31,483
I don't see anything that would
make a spirit mad around here.

233
00:13:31,775 --> 00:13:34,737
Maybe the moon spirit
just turned mean.

234
00:13:35,112 --> 00:13:38,073
The moon spirit is
a gentle, loving lady.

235
00:13:38,157 --> 00:13:40,326
She rules the sky
with compassion.

236
00:13:40,409 --> 00:13:42,578
And... Lunar goodness.

237
00:13:44,330 --> 00:13:46,123
AANG: Excuse me, sir.

238
00:13:46,248 --> 00:13:49,293
Can you tell us anything about
the spirit that's been stealing people?

239
00:13:49,585 --> 00:13:53,756
Only one man ever saw it and
lived, and that's old man Ding.

240
00:13:53,839 --> 00:13:56,300
Where does old man Ding live?

241
00:13:56,383 --> 00:13:59,636
KATARA: Wow, these flowers
are beautiful.

242
00:13:59,762 --> 00:14:01,680
HAMA: They're called fire lilies.

243
00:14:01,764 --> 00:14:04,725
They only bloom
a few weeks a year

244
00:14:04,808 --> 00:14:08,228
but they're one of my favorite
things about living here.

245
00:14:08,312 --> 00:14:12,149
And like all plants, and all
living things, they're filled with water.

246
00:14:12,816 --> 00:14:14,985
I met a waterbender
who lived in a swamp

247
00:14:15,110 --> 00:14:17,613
and could control the vines
by bending the water inside.

248
00:14:18,322 --> 00:14:20,741
You can take it even further.

249
00:14:27,664 --> 00:14:29,666
That was incredible.

250
00:14:31,001 --> 00:14:33,087
It's a shame about
the lilies, though.

251
00:14:33,212 --> 00:14:34,713
They're just flowers.

252
00:14:35,214 --> 00:14:37,466
When you're a waterbender
in a strange land

253
00:14:37,549 --> 00:14:40,010
you do what you must to survive.

254
00:14:40,219 --> 00:14:43,680
Tonight, I'll teach you the ultimate
technique of waterbending.

255
00:14:43,847 --> 00:14:46,975
It can only be done
during the full moon

256
00:14:47,059 --> 00:14:49,186
when your bending
is at its peak.

257
00:14:49,353 --> 00:14:51,355
But isn't that dangerous?

258
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:54,608
I thought people have been disappearing
around here during the full moon.

259
00:14:54,942 --> 00:14:56,402
Oh, Katara.

260
00:14:56,610 --> 00:15:00,114
Two master Waterbenders
beneath a full moon?

261
00:15:00,197 --> 00:15:03,033
I don't think we have
anything to worry about.

262
00:15:13,293 --> 00:15:14,294
AANG: Old man Ding?

263
00:15:14,378 --> 00:15:16,296
Eh, ow...

264
00:15:16,380 --> 00:15:17,673
Aw, dad blame it.

265
00:15:17,756 --> 00:15:18,924
What?

266
00:15:19,007 --> 00:15:20,634
Can't you see I'm busy?

267
00:15:20,717 --> 00:15:22,803
Got a full moon rising.

268
00:15:22,886 --> 00:15:26,765
And why does everyone
call me that, I'm not that old.

269
00:15:26,849 --> 00:15:28,809
[ Grunts ]

270
00:15:29,017 --> 00:15:30,436
Aww...

271
00:15:30,519 --> 00:15:32,479
Well, I'm young at heart.

272
00:15:35,899 --> 00:15:40,988
Not ready to get snapped up
by some moon monster, yet, at least.

273
00:15:41,071 --> 00:15:43,323
SOKKA: We wanted to
ask you about that.

274
00:15:43,407 --> 00:15:45,284
Did you get a good look
at the spirit that took you?

275
00:15:45,367 --> 00:15:47,161
Didn't see no spirit.

276
00:15:47,244 --> 00:15:49,413
Just felt something
come over me.

277
00:15:49,496 --> 00:15:51,331
Like I was possessed.

278
00:15:51,415 --> 00:15:55,419
Forced me to start
walking toward the mountain.

279
00:15:55,752 --> 00:15:59,298
I tried to fight it, but
I couldn't control my own limbs.

280
00:16:00,132 --> 00:16:03,010
It just about had me
into a cave up there.

281
00:16:03,093 --> 00:16:08,807
And I looked up at the moon for what I
thought would be my last glimpse of light.

282
00:16:09,975 --> 00:16:13,270
But then the sun
started to rise.

283
00:16:13,353 --> 00:16:15,647
And I got control of
myself again.

284
00:16:15,731 --> 00:16:19,151
I just high-tailed it away from
that mountain as quick as I could.

285
00:16:19,234 --> 00:16:21,820
Why would a spirit want to
take people to a mountain?

286
00:16:21,904 --> 00:16:23,030
Oh, no!

287
00:16:23,113 --> 00:16:25,532
I did hear people screaming
under the mountain.

288
00:16:25,616 --> 00:16:28,327
The missing villagers
must still be there.

289
00:16:40,255 --> 00:16:42,466
I can hear them,
they're this way.

290
00:16:46,845 --> 00:16:50,098
HAMA: Can you feel the power
the full moon brings?

291
00:16:50,182 --> 00:16:52,559
[ Breathes Deeply ]

292
00:16:52,643 --> 00:16:56,855
For generations, it has blessed
Waterbenders with its glow.

293
00:16:56,939 --> 00:17:00,359
Allowing us to do
incredible things.

294
00:17:02,528 --> 00:17:05,489
I've never felt more alive.

295
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,495
This is the place.

296
00:17:11,578 --> 00:17:13,539
SOKKA: I can't see
anything down there.

297
00:17:13,622 --> 00:17:15,624
TOPH: That's why you have me,
let's go.

298
00:17:29,221 --> 00:17:31,098
We're saved.

299
00:17:31,181 --> 00:17:35,686
I didn't know that spirits made prisons
like this, who brought you here?

300
00:17:35,769 --> 00:17:37,229
It was no spirit.

301
00:17:37,312 --> 00:17:38,939
It was a witch.

302
00:17:39,022 --> 00:17:41,024
A witch, what do you mean?

303
00:17:41,108 --> 00:17:44,027
She seems like
a normal old woman.

304
00:17:44,111 --> 00:17:47,739
But she controls people
like some dark puppetmaster.

305
00:17:47,823 --> 00:17:49,241
Hama.

306
00:17:49,324 --> 00:17:51,368
Yes, the innkeeper.

307
00:17:51,451 --> 00:17:54,162
I knew there was something
creepy about her.

308
00:17:54,329 --> 00:17:55,789
We have to stop Hama.

309
00:17:55,872 --> 00:17:59,209
I'll get these people
out of here, you go.

310
00:17:59,293 --> 00:18:01,920
[ Owl Hoots ]

311
00:18:04,339 --> 00:18:06,133
HAMA: What I'm about to show you

312
00:18:06,216 --> 00:18:09,553
I discovered in that
wretched, Fire Nation prison.

313
00:18:10,679 --> 00:18:14,391
The guards were always careful
to keep any water away from us.

314
00:18:14,641 --> 00:18:18,770
They piped in dry air, and had us
suspended away from the ground.

315
00:18:19,354 --> 00:18:21,064
Before giving us any water,

316
00:18:21,148 --> 00:18:24,526
they would bind our hands and feet
so we couldn't bend.

317
00:18:24,610 --> 00:18:28,488
Any sign of trouble
was met with cruel retribution.

318
00:18:29,364 --> 00:18:33,785
And yet, each month, I felt the full moon
enriching me with its energy.

319
00:18:34,244 --> 00:18:37,623
There had to be something
I could do to escape.

320
00:18:37,789 --> 00:18:42,461
Then I realized that where
there is life, there is water.

321
00:18:42,753 --> 00:18:46,089
The rats that scurried across
the floor of my cage

322
00:18:46,173 --> 00:18:49,509
were nothing more than
skins filled with liquid.

323
00:18:49,593 --> 00:18:54,473
And I passed years developing the skills
that would lead to my escape.

324
00:18:55,515 --> 00:18:57,517
Bloodbending.

325
00:18:57,976 --> 00:19:00,771
Controlling the water
in another body.

326
00:19:00,854 --> 00:19:03,815
Enforcing your own will
over theirs.

327
00:19:04,399 --> 00:19:09,529
Once I had mastered the rats,
I was ready for the men.

328
00:19:09,613 --> 00:19:13,116
[ Grunts ]

329
00:19:16,119 --> 00:19:18,372
HAMA: And during the next
full moon,

330
00:19:18,455 --> 00:19:21,249
I walked free for
the first time in decades.

331
00:19:21,333 --> 00:19:22,501
[ Man Grunts ]

332
00:19:22,584 --> 00:19:26,838
My cell unlocked by the very
guards assigned to keep me in.

333
00:19:27,839 --> 00:19:32,260
Once you perfect this technique,
you can control anything.

334
00:19:32,344 --> 00:19:34,763
Or anyone.

335
00:19:34,846 --> 00:19:38,642
But to reach inside someone
and control them?

336
00:19:38,975 --> 00:19:41,645
I don't know if I want
that kind of power.

337
00:19:41,728 --> 00:19:44,272
The choice is not yours.

338
00:19:44,356 --> 00:19:46,191
The power exists.

339
00:19:46,566 --> 00:19:50,779
And it's your duty to use the gifts
you've been given to win this war.

340
00:19:50,862 --> 00:19:56,243
Katara, they tried to wipe us out,
our entire culture, your mother.

341
00:19:56,326 --> 00:19:57,661
I know.

342
00:19:57,828 --> 00:20:01,289
Then you should understand
what I'm talking about.

343
00:20:01,373 --> 00:20:04,501
We're the last Waterbenders
of the southern tribe.

344
00:20:04,584 --> 00:20:07,713
We have to fight these people
whenever we can.

345
00:20:07,796 --> 00:20:11,133
Wherever they are,
with any means necessary.

346
00:20:12,134 --> 00:20:13,510
It's you.

347
00:20:13,593 --> 00:20:16,930
You're the one who's making people
disappear during the full moons.

348
00:20:17,347 --> 00:20:20,267
They threw me in prison to rot

349
00:20:20,350 --> 00:20:22,686
along with
my brothers and sisters.

350
00:20:22,769 --> 00:20:24,354
They deserve the same.

351
00:20:24,730 --> 00:20:26,732
You must carry on my work.

352
00:20:26,815 --> 00:20:29,234
I won't, I won't
use bloodbending

353
00:20:29,317 --> 00:20:32,028
and I won't allow you
to keep terrorizing this town.

354
00:20:32,112 --> 00:20:33,613
[ Screams ]

355
00:20:33,697 --> 00:20:36,199
[ Grunts... ]

356
00:20:36,283 --> 00:20:40,203
You should have learned the technique
before you turned against me.

357
00:20:40,287 --> 00:20:43,582
It's impossible to fight
your way out of my grip.

358
00:20:43,707 --> 00:20:48,253
I control every muscle,
every vein in your body.

359
00:20:48,336 --> 00:20:53,008
[ Katara Gasps and grunts... ]

360
00:21:01,266 --> 00:21:03,018
Stop, please.

361
00:21:03,101 --> 00:21:08,148
[ Laughs... ]

362
00:21:21,244 --> 00:21:24,331
KATARA: You're not the only one
who draws power from the moon.

363
00:21:24,456 --> 00:21:27,250
My bending is more powerful
than yours, Hama.

364
00:21:27,334 --> 00:21:30,545
Your technique is useless on me.

365
00:21:49,356 --> 00:21:51,441
[ Hama Screams ]

366
00:21:54,986 --> 00:21:56,655
We know what you've
been doing, Hama.

367
00:21:56,988 --> 00:21:58,782
Give up, you're outnumbered.

368
00:21:59,366 --> 00:22:00,909
No.

369
00:22:01,701 --> 00:22:04,496
You've outnumbered yourselves.

370
00:22:04,663 --> 00:22:08,124
[ Aang And Sokka scream ]

371
00:22:13,755 --> 00:22:15,257
SOKKA: Katara, look out!

372
00:22:15,465 --> 00:22:17,342
[ Grunts ]

373
00:22:17,509 --> 00:22:20,136
It's like my brain
has a mind of its own.

374
00:22:20,303 --> 00:22:22,347
Stop it, arm, stop it!

375
00:22:25,350 --> 00:22:27,102
AANG: This feels weird.

376
00:22:27,185 --> 00:22:29,980
[ Aang Grunts ]

377
00:22:30,063 --> 00:22:31,898
I'm sorry, Aang.

378
00:22:31,982 --> 00:22:33,567
AANG: It's ok.

379
00:22:36,152 --> 00:22:39,281
[ Sokka Grunts ]

380
00:22:39,364 --> 00:22:40,949
[ Sokka Screams ]

381
00:22:41,032 --> 00:22:43,535
Don't hurt your friends, Katara.

382
00:22:43,618 --> 00:22:46,162
And don't let them
hurt each other.

383
00:22:46,246 --> 00:22:48,498
[ Aang And Sokka scream ]

384
00:22:48,582 --> 00:22:49,875
No!

385
00:22:54,254 --> 00:22:58,174
[ Grunts And gasps... ]

386
00:23:11,771 --> 00:23:14,566
You're going to be
locked away forever.

387
00:23:14,649 --> 00:23:16,943
HAMA: My work is done.

388
00:23:17,777 --> 00:23:20,155
Congratulations, Katara.

389
00:23:20,780 --> 00:23:22,991
You're a bloodbender.

390
00:23:24,784 --> 00:23:28,538
[ Laughs... ]

391
00:23:32,208 --> 00:23:36,212
[ Katara Cries... ]

392
00:23:44,763 --> 00:23:49,309
[ ♪... ]
